      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1893 the company reorganized as Ōsaka Breweries, reflecting its deep roots in Osaka’s brewing tradition.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asahi_Breweries",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By 2011 Asahi Breweries became a holding company, creating Asahi Group Holdings and separating its brewing arm.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asahi_Breweries",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Asahi holds a 37% share of Japan’s beer market, the largest among the country’s four major brewers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asahi_Breweries",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 1990 Asahi acquired a 19.9% stake in Australian brewer Elders IXL, later part of Foster’s Group.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
